    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 133.799, 564.088, 477.591, 646.352 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We aim to prove Theorem 2 by induction n. Clearly it is enough to show Theorem 2 for all induced subgraphs of ΛU. The base cases are when n ≤ 7, which are easily veriﬁed. For the inductive step, suppose n ≥ 8 and ΛU[S] is an n-vertex subgraph of ΛU with e edges. Additionally, suppose ΛU[S] has the maximum number of edges out of all n-vertex subgraphs of ΛU. The inductive hypothesis is that all n′-vertex subgraphs of ΛU, where 3 ≤ n′ < n, have at most e(n′) edges."
  }, {
    "type" : "list",
    "pdfua_tag" : "L",
    "id" : 29,
    "level" : "1",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 133.799, 197.038, 477.502, 554.672 ],
